{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"861700807626588220","content":"You go from tree to tree hearing him talking in an unknown language","created_at":"2021-08-21T16:14:55.146000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"878673532639395900","reply_to_id":"878673256494796851","thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"mazie","id":"366565198284324868","is_bot":0,"username":"damnzam"},"author_id":"366565198284324868","channel_id":"861700807626588220","content":"`Stop being so cute about it. Dammit. Colorful flowers. That's adorable.`\n\nHe ruffles his feathers again.\n\n`In an old culture, those union rites are for the people who truly believe their bond transcends their existence as individuals. Lovers, friends, siblings, soulmates. And they find something to prove it, an object that represents them.`\n\n`If you wanna complicate things a bit, there's also how on the night of the ritual, the community lets that object go on the waves or the current, and the couple spend a whole month alone trying to find it. But uh, the rivers here are a hazard. I preach safety over reviving an old practice.`","created_at":"2021-08-21T16:17:11.684000Z","edited_at":"2021-08-21T16:18:58.881000Z","id":"878674105321275392","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"861700807626588220","content":"'Understandable. Especially when only... half of us two can swim. Or a bit more if you count Kukudh as separate from me, but.'","created_at":"2021-08-21T16:19:46.746000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"878674755698446357","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
